<section class="phero"><div class="phero-bg"><img src="/assets/img/photos/tornado-field.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/tornado-field-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/tornado-field.webp 1023w" sizes="100vw" width="1023" height="685" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" data-parallax="0.18"></div><div class="wrap phero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><ol><li><a href="/">Home</a></li><li><a href="/claim-appraisal-services/">Services</a></li><li>Tornado &amp; Wind Damage Appraisal</li></ol></nav><p class="kicker kicker-l">Appraisal service</p><h1>Tornado Damage Appraisal and Wind Claim Valuation</h1><p class="lede">Arkansas sits in the path of spring and late-fall tornado outbreaks, and straight-line winds from summer storm complexes do damage just as real. Wind claims are often bigger and messier than they first appear.</p><div class="row"><a class="btn btn-red" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> Call (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-ghost-w" href="/contact-an-appraiser/">Free claim review</a></div><ul class="facts"><li><small>Peak</small><b>March–May, Nov–Dec</b></li><li><small>Includes</small><b>Straight-line wind</b></li><li><small>Scope</small><b>Structure to finishes</b></li></ul></div></section>
<div class="wrap two"><article class="prose">
<p>Tornadoes have struck Arkansas communities many times in recent memory: the April 2014 tornado through Mayflower and Vilonia, the March 2020 tornado in Jonesboro, and the March 31, 2023 tornadoes that crossed west Little Rock into North Little Rock and devastated Wynne the same afternoon. In each case, homes just outside the worst damage path had claims that looked minor at first and grew as walls were opened.</p>
<h2>Damage that hides after a wind event</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Racked framing.</strong> Doors and windows that stick, drywall cracks at corners and gaps at trim can signal that the structure shifted.</li>
<li><strong>Uplifted roof decking.</strong> Shingles may lie back down while nails have backed out and seal strips have broken.</li>
<li><strong>Debris impacts.</strong> Siding, brick veneer, windows and HVAC units struck by flying debris on every elevation, not just the obvious one.</li>
<li><strong>Water intrusion.</strong> Rain that followed the wind into attics and wall cavities, with mold risk if it isn’t dried out quickly.</li>
<li><strong>Fences, outbuildings and trees.</strong> Other-structures coverage and debris removal limits often go unclaimed.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Our approach</h2>
<p>We document the structure first: framing, sheathing, foundation anchoring and roof-to-wall connections. Then we scope finishes room by room. Where needed, we recommend a structural engineer and include that report in the appraisal record. If a home is a total loss, we focus on whether the replacement-cost valuation reflects what it actually costs to rebuild in that county today.</p>
<h2>Straight-line winds count too</h2>
<p>Summer storm complexes can push winds past 70 mph across the Delta and central Arkansas without a tornado. Wind is wind under most policies, and the claim deserves the same full scope.</p>
<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Does it matter whether a tornado was confirmed?<svg class="chev" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Not usually. Most policies cover windstorm damage regardless of whether the National Weather Service rated a tornado.</p></div></details><details><summary>My home is a total loss. What is there to appraise?<svg class="chev" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>The replacement-cost value, debris removal, code upgrades, other structures and contents can all be disputed on a total loss.</p></div></details><details><summary>Do you work after big outbreaks when everyone is busy?<svg class="chev" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Yes. After a major event we prioritize files with approaching deadlines and active water intrusion.</p></div></details></div>
<h2>Related services</h2><div class="rel3"><a class="pcard rv" href="/claim-appraisal-services/hurricane-remnant-wind-appraisal/"><span class="pcard-ph"><img src="/assets/img/photos/snapped-tree.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/snapped-tree-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/snapped-tree.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, 260px" width="1200" height="900" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></span><span class="pcard-b"><h3>Hurricane Remnant &amp; Tropical Storm Claims</h3><span class="pcard-p">Gulf hurricanes can still bring damaging wind and rain to south Arkansas days after landfall.</span><span class="more">Learn more <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M4 12h15M13 5l7 7-7 7"/></svg></span></span></a><a class="pcard rv" href="/claim-appraisal-services/water-damage-claim-appraiser/"><span class="pcard-ph"><img src="/assets/img/photos/kitchen.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/kitchen-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/kitchen.webp 1024w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, 260px" width="1024" height="683" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></span><span class="pcard-b"><h3>Water Damage Claim Appraisal</h3><span class="pcard-p">Burst pipes, appliance leaks and storm water inside the home, valued to a full and dry repair.</span><span class="more">Learn more <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M4 12h15M13 5l7 7-7 7"/></svg></span></span></a><a class="pcard rv" href="/claim-appraisal-services/fire-smoke-loss-appraisal/"><span class="pcard-ph"><img src="/assets/img/photos/house-fire.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/house-fire-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/house-fire.webp 1023w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, 260px" width="1023" height="806" alt="" load